{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-213817","model_call":54,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2119"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2119"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_308833481#13_705003389","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2119","rank":3,"snippet":"Work U.S. & World Economies Economic Terms Sin Taxes, Their Pros and Cons, and Whether They Work If Wine Is Taxed, Why Isn't Soda? Key Takeaways Federal Sin Taxes State Sin Taxes Pros Cons History Article Sources \" , \"segment\": \"A 10% tax reduces smoking among those aged 12 to 17 by 11.9%. 10 ﻿ Why do states want to reduce smoking? Lung cancer is the leading cause of cancer death. Between 80% and 90% of lung cancer deaths are due to smoking. 11 ﻿ <cover>Kentucky, the state with the highest tobacco use, has one of the highest rates of lung cancer. 12 ﻿ Sin taxes help states </cover>pay the cost of treating the public health consequences of smoking, drinking, and gambling. But states don’t spend as much of this tax revenue on health care as they could. It covers some of society's cost of educating people about lung cancer. Sin taxes are more politically viable than raising income or sales taxes. According to the Campaign for Tobacco-Free Kids, national and state opinion polls have \"consistently shown broad voter support\" for tobacco tax increases.\" , \"start_char\": 5050.000000","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1452682537#5_3268424250","rank":1,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1452682537#4_3268422067","rank":2,"relevance":2}]},"time":7},"model_calls":54,"document_judgments":44,"relevance_3":21,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
